* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary

# What belongs to the workshop, not to the program.
#
# The source archive GitHub builds from a branch or a tag is what people
# download and what an update installs, so it should hold Sourcerer and nothing
# else. export-ignore is honoured by `git archive`, which is what GitHub's
# "Source code (zip)" is made with. Nothing here affects a clone, and the
# workflow still runs: Actions checks the repository out.
/.github         export-ignore
/.gitattributes  export-ignore
/.gitignore      export-ignore
/.claude         export-ignore
# The brand guide and the social preview are for GitHub, not for the program; the README's two banners (SVG) go with it, or its picture is broken.
/Sourcerer_files/docs/brand/*.png export-ignore
